                   BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Revising Procedural Deadlines                           Docket No. 25-00079-UT



        7.      The Hearing Examiners also find good and sufficient cause to commence the

hearing on the stipulation on July 13, 2026.

IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

        A.      The Joint Motion is GRANTED.

        B.      The June 16, 2026, deadline for filing rebuttal testimony is VACATED.

        C.      Subject to paragraph D, below, all remaining interim deadlines are VACATED,

including any deadlines for motions in limine, motions to strike testimony, other testimony-related

or non-testimony-related prehearing motions, and responses to those motions.

        D.      This Order does not preclude any party from filing motions necessary to implement,

support, oppose, or obtain Commission review of the stipulation, including motions addressing

confidentiality, admission of evidence, hearing procedures, or other matters related to the

stipulation.

        E.      The deadline to file the stipulation is June 22, 2026.

        F.      The deadline to file statements of opposition to the stipulation is June 29, 2026.

        G.      If a contested stipulation is filed, the deadline to file testimony in support of the

stipulation is June 30, 2026.

        H.      If a contested stipulation is filed, the deadline to file testimony in opposition to the

stipulation is July 7, 2026, before 12:00 p.m. MT.

        I.      If a contested stipulation is filed, the deadline to file rebuttal testimony in support

of the stipulation is July 9, 2026.

        J.      If an uncontested comprehensive stipulation is filed, the deadline to file testimony

in support of the stipulation is July 2, 2026.


                                                 -3-
                   BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Revising Procedural Deadlines                           Docket No. 25-00079-UT



        K.       All signatories to the filed stipulation shall file testimony in support of the

stipulation.

        L.       A hearing on the stipulation shall begin on July 13, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. MT, and

continue as necessary through July 17, 2026.

        M.       A prehearing conference shall be held on July 7, 2026, at 2:00 p.m. MT.

        N.       A Zoom invitation including the link to access the prehearing shall be sent to all

parties on the existing service list. If a party wishes to attend and has not received the Zoom

invitation     with   the   link    by   that   time,    please   contact   Ana   Kippenbrock      at

Ana.Kippenbrock@prc.nm.gov.

        O.       All other procedural requirements not inconsistent with this Order remain in effect.

        ISSUED under the Seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on June 18, 2026.



                                   NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION




